   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "«Molto» as an invariable adverb",
     "texto": [
      "When it modifies an **adjective**, another **adverb** or a **verb**, *molto* works as an adverb and is **strictly invariable**: **Lei è molto stanca** (she is very tired); **Lavorano molto bene** (they work very well); **Mangio molto** (I eat a lot). One never says *molta stanca*."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "«Molto» as a variable adjective",
     "texto": [
      "When it quantifies a **noun**, it works as an indefinite adjective and **must agree** in gender and number: **molto tempo** (a lot of time), **molta pazienza** (a lot of patience), **molti libri** (many books), **molte amiche** (many female friends)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "The double behaviour of «molto»",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "Grammatical function",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Concordancia",
       "lengua": "estudio"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Model examples",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
     "filas": [
      [
       {
        "texto": "Adverb (with adjective or verb)",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "Invariable (always ends in -o)",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "Sono molto contenta. / Mangia molto.",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "texto": "Adjective (with a masculine noun)",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
